// Title: Unusual Child Process of dns.exe
// Sigma ID: a4e3d776-f12e-42c2-8510-9e6ed1f43ec3
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Tim Rauch, Elastic (idea)
// Date: 2022-09-27 | Modified: 2023-02-05
// ATT&CK: persistence, initial-access, T1133
// Description: Detects an unexpected process spawning from dns.exe which may indicate activity related to
//   remote code execution or other forms of exploitation as seen in CVE-2020-1350 (SigRed)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/unusual-child-process-of-dns-exe.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_dns_susp_child_process.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\dns.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\conhost.exe"))
